The ZIP and ZIPOPT variables of the environment: each backslash was removed with
strcpy() of a string onto itself shifted by one (overlapping strings: undefined
behaviour; the string functions of the libc of FreeBSD 15 copy in blocks and may
garble the arguments). memmove(), as RHEL 10 carries it (sast.patch of zip 3.0,
RHEL-44659), with the length corrected: strlen(argstart + 1) + 1, the bytes from
there to the terminating NUL (that of RHEL, strlen(argstart) + 1, read one byte past
it). The same fix as unzip-6.0-sast.patch of archivers/unzip for its envargs.c.

--- util.c.orig
+++ util.c
@@ -862,7 +862,7 @@
 
             /* remove escape characters */
             while ((argstart = MBSCHR(argstart, '\\')) != NULL) {
-                strcpy(argstart, argstart + 1);
+                memmove(argstart, argstart + 1, strlen(argstart + 1) + 1);
                 if (*argstart)
                     ++argstart;
             }
